  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 758868,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1 on 1 (Sony PlayStation) - Synopsis\n\n*1 on 1* is a unique and energetic sports game for the PlayStation, blending basketball with fighting game mechanics. Released in 1998, it distinguishes itself with its over-the-top, anime-inspired visuals and a focus on individual player rivalries rather than team play. \n\nPlayers choose from a roster of eccentric characters, each possessing distinct special moves and unique basketball skills. Gameplay revolves around fast-paced one-on-one matches, where players must utilize a combination of dribbling, passing, shooting, and powerful special attacks to outmaneuver and defeat their opponents. \n\nBeyond the core basketball action, *1 on 1* introduces a combat system allowing players to unleash devastating blows and signature moves. The game's vibrant presentation, coupled with its unconventional gameplay, creates a chaotic and entertaining experience that stands out from traditional sports titles. It's a celebration of individual skill and a showcase of over-the-top action."
    },
